notes: "After the change is saved, anyone can open its record, and this is where to find it. 1, the Activity panel lists every saved writer receipt with the slides it touched; Review changes opens it. 2, the receipt says which operation it was, who made it and when: here, Claude Code at 10:53 in the evening. 3, Before and After show the actual slide in both states. 4, Saved changes lists every object and field that was written: the slide chart and its two axis titles removed, the new figure added, the title, the lead, the speaker notes and the Story. This dialog is read-only. If you want the old slide back, you restore a named version from History, which affects only that slide. Changes from people and from agents arrive through the same writer, so they are reviewed in the same way."
